<%- include('../../partials/policy-start') %>
<p class="lead">We want you to buy with confidence. If the course isn’t right for you, you can get your money back. Here’s how it works.</p>

<div class="callout"><strong>The short version:</strong> a full refund within 14 days of purchase, as long as you haven’t started the final exam.</div>

<h2>Full refund</h2>
<p>You can have a full refund if <strong>both</strong> of these are true:</p>
<ul>
  <li>you ask within <strong>14 days</strong> of your purchase, and</li>
  <li>you haven’t started the final exam (starting the check-in counts as starting it).</li>
</ul>
<p>It doesn’t matter how many chapters or quizzes you’ve completed.</p>

<h2>When we can’t refund</h2>
<ul>
  <li>After the final exam has been started, or a certificate has been issued.</li>
  <li>When an exam attempt was voided, or an account closed, because the <a href="/exam-policy">exam rules</a> or <a href="/terms">terms of use</a> weren’t followed.</li>
  <li>More than 14 days after purchase.</li>
</ul>
<p>These limits don’t affect any right to a refund you have under consumer protection law.</p>

<h2>Problems on our side</h2>
<p>If a fault in our system stops you completing the exam, we’ll restore your attempt so you can take it again. If we can’t fix the problem, we’ll refund you in full, whenever it happened. If you were charged twice for the same course, we refund the duplicate payment straight away.</p>

<h2>How to ask for a refund</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> from the address on your account.</li>
  <li>Include your learner ID (HV-L-…) and payment reference (HV-P-…). Both are in your enrolment email, and your learner ID is on your account page.</li>
  <li>We reply within two business days. Approved refunds go back to the card you paid with. Your bank usually shows them within 5 to 10 business days.</li>
</ol>
<p>When a refund is issued, your access to the course ends.</p>
<%- include('../../partials/policy-end') %>
